WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
 Say, boys and girls, I'd like to show you this wonderful Mary Hartline magic doll that the Kellogg's folks have for you.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.220
 See? She looks just like me.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:18.920
 She's made out of sturdy plastic board, one inch of an inch thick, stands nine inches high in her own plastic stand, and she comes in crude to light color.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.360
 But the most wonderful thing about this magic doll is she really is magic.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:33.600
 You just cut out one of these cute costumes, slide it back and forth a couple of times like this, and the costume will stick right on magically.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.820
 No tap, no paste.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.840
 And with the magic doll, you get ten beautiful true color outfits.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.040
 Everything from shorts to a beautiful pink formal.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.020
 Why, even two of my own super circus costumes.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:01:00.200
 And kids, you can get this terrific Mary Hartline magic doll just by sending in 25 cents in coin and a box top from Kellogg's Sugar Smacks or Kellogg's Sugar Frosted Flakes.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:09.160
 Use the handy order blank on the package or send direct to Mary Hartline doll, box 313, Battle Creek, Michigan.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.440
 That's Mary Hartline magic doll, box 313, Battle Creek, Michigan.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.880
 That's the prettiest cutout doll ever and such fun to play with.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.980
 So send for your Mary Hartline magic doll right away.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:30.840
 Mary Hartline magic doll, box 313, Battle Creek, Michigan.

